<p>In other words, about two-thirds of recorded hail reports in the county were quarter size or larger, and more than a third reached golf ball size. That partly reflects how reports are collected: larger hail is more likely to be noticed and reported. Still, it shows that when hail does fall here, it is frequently big enough to matter.</p>

