<p>The April 20, 2012 storm stands out for McAllen. The NWS narrative describes softball-size hail reported by the public at McAllen High School, with golf ball to baseball size stones falling for more than twenty minutes as the storm moved across the McAllen and Mission area. (On the SPC conversion table, 4.00 inches is softball size and 4.50 inches is grapefruit size; the NWS record for this event describes the stones as softball size.) More recently, the April 21, 2023 storm brought up to an hour of continuous hail across southern Hidalgo County, and on May 8, 2025, a supercell produced 3-inch hail in north McAllen.</p>

